By default Spring doesn't throw an exception for unknown URLs; it just returns Tomcat's 404 page. Turn that on.

If your WebAppInitializer extends AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer, add:

@Override
protected void customizeRegistration(javax.servlet.ServletRegistration.Dynamic registration) {
    registration.setInitParameter("throwExceptionIfNoHandlerFound", "true");
}



If it implements WebApplicationInitializer and creates the dispatcher itself, add this line after ServletRegistration.Dynamic dispatcher = ...:

dispatcher.setInitParameter("throwExceptionIfNoHandlerFound", "true");
